<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Agent mark — a ghost silhouette.

  Drawn on a plain 24x24 viewport so a 22dp call site shows a mark that fills
  22dp. The previous `ic_agent_mark.xml` used a 2048 viewport with a group
  transform to rescale the artwork, which existed because that source drawing
  only occupied 46% of its canvas — the empty viewport, not the icon size, was
  the original problem, and it needed a comment three paragraphs long to
  explain. This one is drawn at the size it is used.

  Silhouette rather than an outline: a filled body reads at 22dp, a stroked one
  turns to mush. The eyes and the wavy hem are cut as holes with evenOdd
  instead of being painted in a second colour, because Icon() applies a single
  ColorFilter over the whole drawable — two paint colours collapse to one the
  moment it is tinted, and the features vanish into the body. A hole cannot be
  filled by a tint.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24"
    android:tint="?android:attr/colorControlNormal">

    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:fillType="evenOdd"
